WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:07.285
Welcome to One DSD People, Access and Culture.
Whether you're a director, manager, supervisor,

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.205
or staff member, this is a place to

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.525
connect equity with your everyday work.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:15.765
You can build understanding, prepare for a
decision, or find a useful resource.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.100
Learning here is voluntary. Start where you are,
and explore at your own pace.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.635
Choose Enter One DSD to reach the home

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.135
page. Beneath the photograph, three starting

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.995
paths help you find your way.

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.455
Learn introduces courses and examples.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:33.875
Apply takes you to the Equity Analysis Toolkit.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:36.295
Connect helps you find guidance and support.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.910
You do not have to work through everything in
order.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:47.895
If you are unsure where to begin, choose Connect
learning with work near the top of

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:49.935
the page. Start with something you need to

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:53.915
understand, a decision you're considering, or a
change you want to learn from.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:57.570
The five connected areas below offer more detail
when you need it.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:05.075
For disability services work, explore DSD

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:08.155
programs and services. Find a relevant service,

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:12.295
then open Equity question and resources. These
connections help you consider the people

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.355
involved, possible barriers, and useful

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:17.115
guidance. DSD sits within the Aging and

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:22.515
Disability Services Administration, or ADSA.
Keep your own responsibilities and the relevant

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:24.310
requirements in view.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.375
In Learning and resources, search for a question

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:36.575
or choose a theme. Foundation, Intermediate, and
Advanced describe learning depth, not your job

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.575
title. Look for what a course helps you

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.815
practice and prepare. You can explore team

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.395
collaboration, policy work, communication, and

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:46.890
other topics, choosing what is useful for the
work ahead.

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:55.415
Need a tool right now? Visit the resource
library. Search for a topic,

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:57.775
or follow a theme into learning, tools, and

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.255
guidance. The links also lead to books and

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:04.795
research, and recordings and podcasts. You can
use a practical resource directly and

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:06.910
return to a course when it would help.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:14.755
To see the wider purpose, open People, Access

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:19.775
and Culture in practice from the home page. The
first video introduces the Equity Outcome

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:22.775
Map. The second follows DSD examples connected

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:27.375
to the six ADSA goals. Beside the examples,
links show which existing

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:30.210
tools can help you take the next step.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:37.595
The Equity Analysis Toolkit helps you examine a

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:42.095
decision. Consider who is affected, what the
evidence supports, and which alternatives

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:44.995
deserve attention. The fictional notice example

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.775
makes one distinction clear: sending information

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.315
does not establish that people understood it.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:54.870
Watch the reasoning, then try a different
situation or begin your own working draft.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:01.635
Resources can help you prepare thoughtful

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:06.855
questions. Minnesota Communities offers context,
and the cultural and language-access guidance

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:11.055
helps you consider participation. Use them
alongside conversations with the people

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.755
affected. A resource cannot tell you what every

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:18.650
person needs, and a prepared analysis does not
replace the responsible decision-maker.

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:28.195
Begin with one question from your work. Choose
one resource, try something useful, and

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.915
return to what happened. What became clearer?

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.775
Who could participate more fully?

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.375
What still needs attention? One DSD is here

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:38.750
to help you keep learning and bring that
learning into practice.
